package main

// These fields belong to the WebGPU renderer's state objects (timingState,
// meshState, uniformState, gpuRes, pipeState, selenaState, waterState,
// drawState, telemetryState and the root record), and esbuild renames them in
// bootstrap-feature-scene3d-webgpu.js only. esbuild shortens local variables
// but never properties, so the split that moved closure variables onto those
// objects grew the chunk until this list gave the bytes back.
//
// The list holds the names that the factory writes into those objects, and
// that no other code reads or writes by name. A name stays off the list when:
//
//   - a quoted string of that name appears in the chunk's sources (a dynamic
//     or string key, such as canvas, draw, frame, waterState, waterSystems,
//     temporalAA, autoExposure and the three mesh buffers);
//   - a test reads it as a property of the running renderer, its stats or its
//     diagnostics (device, mount, queue, gpuRes, pipeState, selenaState,
//     uniformState, textureCache, the water pipelines and the like);
//   - it is short (under four letters), because a short name is likely to
//     meet an unrelated property of the same name;
//   - another chunk uses it as a property name.
//     TestWebGPURenamedPropertiesStayInsideTheWebGPUChunk enforces this rule,
//     as the WebGL test does for its chunk. Four names left the list for it:
//     initError and initFailed (the Scene3D mount reads them), skyResources
//     (the WebGL renderer has the same field) and thickLineScratch (the scene
//     math chunk has it).
//
// The renderer's public fields (kind, texturePreparation, textureVariantContext
// and the methods it returns) and the keys of diagnostics() are not on the
// list. Keep this allowlist explicit: a blanket pattern would rename fields
// that leave the chunk.
